# PART 5 — MULTI-PRODUCT ENQUIRY BASKET

## 11. Implement a trade enquiry basket

Allow buyers to add multiple commodities to one RFQ instead of submitting a separate enquiry for every product.

This is a business enquiry basket, not a shopping cart. Do not introduce checkout, payments or public product prices.

### Required functionality

- Add a commodity from catalogue cards.
- Add a commodity from its detail page.
- Display the current selected products.
- Remove individual products.
- Change the requested quantity and unit where supported.
- Select available grade, variety or processing options.
- Edit product-specific requirements.
- Display an appropriate empty state.
- Continue browsing without losing the basket.
- Open the RFQ form with all selected products.
- Review the complete request before submission.
- Submit all selected products as one enquiry.

### User experience

- Show a compact basket indicator in the header when appropriate.
- On mobile, keep the basket easy to access without overcrowding the header.
- Provide clear visual feedback when an item is added.
- Prevent duplicate entries for the same product and compatible options.
- Allow genuinely different product variants to remain separate.
- Make removing or editing an item straightforward.

### State persistence

Inspect the existing application and choose an appropriate persistence mechanism.

For anonymous visitors, local browser storage may be used for non-sensitive basket selections if consistent with the application and applicable privacy requirements.

Do not store passwords, credentials or sensitive personal information in browser storage.

For authenticated users, server-side persistence may be appropriate if the existing architecture supports it.

The basket must survive normal navigation and refreshes according to the chosen implementation.

### Data consistency

- Use actual product IDs or stable identifiers.
- Revalidate product availability and supported options on the server when submitting an RFQ.
- Never trust client-provided product prices or specifications.
- Do not fabricate unavailable product data.

